SUMMARY:Walk at Grover Cleveland Park
DESCRIPTION:Let's Walk!!\n**MEETING TIME 10 AM**\n\nWe will meet near the 
 fishing pond entrance of the park\, close to Brookside Avenue and the boat
  house/restrooms.\n**GPS location: 138 Brookside Ave\, Caldwell. Park on t
 he street.**\n\nWe will walk for about 60-90 minutes at about a 3 miles/ho
 ur pace. The park has a paved path loop that is a little more than a mile.
  Stay for as many loops as you like.\n\nGrover Cleveland Park in Caldwell/
 Essex Fells celebrated its centennial in 2013. As the first county park in
  western Essex County\, the site was originally selected for its natural b
 eauty and its potential to provide a space for relaxation and recreation. 
 It contains gentle rolling hills\, broad meadows and other environmentally
  aesthetic features\n\n**Please arrive 5 minutes early\, so we can start o
 n time.**\n\nFOLLOW US ON INSTAGRAM - letswalkmeetup\n\nDisclaimer: If you
  join us for a hike\, please understand that you are responsible for your 
 own preparedness and well-being and will hold no one else liable in case o
 f injury or mishap. Event will be canceled in the event of extreme weather
 .
